    {
      "id": 223,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Areas scaled to 0",
      "description": "How many areas of this instance, and the console, are set to run zero pods. This is a state, not a fault: an area at zero was scaled down by hand (kubectl scale with --replicas=0), for example paused for maintenance, so it is shown in blue, it does not count as down, and no alert fires for it. It sits apart from Areas with no pod available, which counts areas that want pods and have none. An area scaled to zero stops reporting its own readiness and metrics, so this tile is where it still shows. If you did not mean to scale an area to zero, scale it back.",
